From 50d7558b63f66f99c627db6c016fa1709459b345 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LegendaryFire <tristan.balon@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 02:21:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Read Inkling 2's NVFP4 expert rows with every lane busy in
 decode

The decode expert kernels left lanes idle at Inkling's shapes: the
gate/up rows (n_embd 2304: 72 halves of NVFP4 blocks) took the
generic multi kernel's warp a row, its last pass with 8 of 32 lanes;
the down rows (n_ff 1152: 18 blocks) took 8 lanes a row with 6 busy.
Now each lane takes halves (32 values: one q8_1 block, two UE4M3
sub-blocks):

- gate/up, native_gu_nv4_kernel: 8 lanes a row, 9 halves each, 4 rows
  a warp; the group's entries' q8_1 rows staged in shared memory, a
  lane's weights loaded before its dots (all in flight), 3 blocks an
  SM (80 registers): 85.0 -> 75.8 us at one row;
- down, native_down_nv4_kernel: 4 lanes a row, 9 halves each, 8 rows a
  warp: 44.4 -> 42.8 us.

vec_dot_nvfp4_q8_1's sums in another lane order (within ~1e-7 of the
reference kernels; a down input's q8_1 rounding now and then one step
apart). Two cards, decode without drafting: 1K 51.6 -> 52.6 tok/s,
60K 44.0 -> 45.0, 180K 31.3 -> 31.5.
